# Citation metadata, in the Citation File Format.
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub reads this file to offer a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo
# reads it when minting a DOI for a release. Keep `version` and `date-released`
# in step with the release tag: a citation that does not name a version cannot
# be checked against the results it produced.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "G-Synth: PCR-free gene synthesis and cloning design with verified assembly"
message: "If you use this software in published work, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Merzoug
    given-names: Mohamed
    email: mohamed.merzoug.essbo@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Genomics Technology Platform, Higher School of Biological Sciences
      of Oran (ESSBO), Oran, Algeria

repository-code: "https://github.com/Midotech31/g-synth-app"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"

abstract: >-
  G-Synth automates a laboratory gene synthesis and cloning workflow: codon
  optimisation that provably preserves the protein, PCR-free oligo assembly
  with orthogonal overhangs (Merzoug assembly), in-silico cloning into a
  vector, and verification of the result against Sanger traces. Designs are
  re-ligated in silico on both strands and checked against the sticky ends the
  chosen restriction enzymes leave before they can be exported, so no oligo
  set is issued that has not been simulated end to end.

keywords:
  - gene synthesis
  - molecular cloning
  - codon optimisation
  - restriction enzymes
  - oligonucleotide assembly
  - synthetic biology
  - Sanger sequencing verification
  - bioinformatics
